            3. What Are Garage Floor Tiles Made Of?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Most garage tiles are rigid polypropylene or flexible PVC, with rubber as a third option used mainly in gyms. Rigid tiles are usually polypropylene or a polypropylene copolymer: hard, light and stiff, with hooks and loops molded into their edges. Flexible tiles are usually PVC: heavier, softer and quieter, joined either by dovetail edges or by an adhesive back. Each one behaves differently once a car rolls onto it.
          </p>

