          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most garages with daily parking, Swisstrax Ribtrax Pro is the tile to buy: vented, stiff and well finished, with the accessories that make the edges look professional. RaceDeck Diamond fits dry show garages, IncStores Nitro and DiamondTrax Home fit tighter budgets, Gladiator is the convenient local purchase, and G-Floor RaceDay peel-and-stick fits a quiet, smooth floor you do not plan to move.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you pick, clean the slab, leave room for expansion, order extras from one batch and keep jack stands off bare tiles. Tiles are not the cheapest garage floor, but they are the most forgiving, and on a slab that would never hold a coating they are often the only floor that still looks good years later.
